The cut divides combined data into left (i + j elements) and right (m+n-i-j). For the median we need i + j = ⌈(m+n)/2⌉, and (m+n+1)//2 IS that ceiling in integer arithmetic — the +1 makes ODD totals put the extra element on the left, so the median is max(left side); even totals average the two middle boundaries. i and j are COUNTS of elements on the left (while A[i] and B[j] are VALUES, 0-based) — so j is derived, not probed: j = (m+n+1)//2 - i falls out of the count equation. Edge cuts (i=0 or i=m) use ∓∞ sentinels so the comparisons stay well-defined. The +1 is THE classic off-by-one of this problem — get the half equation right and the whole solution falls out. =====================================================================

