parent[x] chains x to its component root; find() flattens the path; union() attaches the smaller-rank root under the larger. With both optimisations the amortised cost is the INVERSE ACKERMANN function α(n) — ≤ 4 for any practical n. Node labels are 0..n−1 so plain arrays index directly — no hash table needed (Python dict probing h(k,i)=(hash(k)+i) mod m is only for sparse/arbitrary labels). =====================================================================

