P(t) = "path exists at water level t" is monotone because water never goes DOWN: reachable at t ⇒ reachable at t+1. Any monotone predicate on a sorted universe answers with binary search in O(log H) probes — each probe a graph reachability run. The DSU variant unions flooded cells instead of visiting them one by one; connectivity then costs two find() calls. BFS proves an actual path, DSU proves connectivity — both answer the same question. ---------------------------------------------------------------------

The predicate P(t) = "path exists at water level t" is monotone because water never goes DOWN: if the set of cells reachable at level t contains the target, it also contains it at level t+1. Any monotone predicate on a sorted universe answers with binary search in O(log H) probes — here each probe is a graph reachability run. DSU variant: instead of visiting cells one by one, we UNION underwater cells with their underwater neighbours; connectivity then costs two finds. BFS probes the actual path, DSU probes only connectivity — both answer the same question. ===================================================================== /

